comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-06T21:57:53.338Z",maintainer-agent,"Audit #15 scope note: test-all is also a bulk variant of a base noun and belongs in this fold (pm test --all, mirroring update-many->update --many). Include it in the mapping + alias shim so no bulk spelling stays top-level."
  "2026-09-09T21:40:15.686Z","harness:codex","Selection evidence 2026-09-09: strict all-status CLI read returned all 2728 items with complete status, no omissions, no truncation, and no unreadable items. Reusing pm-ik19 and pm-eq4x, with accepted grammar and alias lineage pm-pbyu, pm-0z7n and pm-hb7ug8. GitHub CLI inventory found zero open PRs, issues, Dependabot alerts, code-scanning alerts and secret-scanning alerts. Existing history restore and ops test-all placements will be verified as part of lifecycle parity."
  "2026-09-09T21:58:48.339Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: canonical paths are update many, close many and close delete. Existing history restore and ops test-all placements retain accepted ADR ownership. SDK alias metadata drives native operation resolution, flags, capability routing and completions. Sandbox regression verifies native/legacy dry-run equality followed by actual update, close, delete, restore and strict history verification."
  "2026-09-09T22:09:57.410Z","harness:codex","Graph evidence: native close many regression reuses the existing rollback suite from pm-7p4w and verifies the per-item close contract introduced by pm-i17g. Added verifies edges preserve their historical completion and make the delivered behavior discoverable from the current grammar implementation. Capability routing now advertises canonical history paths while hiding compatibility aliases."
  "2026-09-09T22:19:41.169Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: packaged CLI installed and passed isolated create, claim --start, release --pause, update many, close --release-assignment, close delete dry-run and strict history verification with npm and Bun. Docs/skills full gate and unchanged flag/help-token budget gate now pass. Full-suite run exposed stale test expectations and concurrent-build imports; those are being resolved before a stable full coverage rerun."
  "2026-09-09T22:45:52.553Z","harness:codex","Verification update: both linked test commands passed. Live grammar census, positional signatures, flag invocation parity, flag/help budgets, recovery replay, MCP deprecations, graph-composition and record-integrity assurances passed. The latest GitHub inventory remains empty for PRs, issues, Dependabot, code scanning and secret scanning. Final exact coverage and quiet import-cost verification are pending before reviewed closure."
  "2026-09-09T23:01:35.068Z","harness:codex","Final local verification: the full 657-file, 8656-test suite passed with exact 100/100/100/100 all-source coverage and zero uncovered counts. Native/legacy bulk parity, actual mutation and restore, rollback checkpoints, named item ids, four-shell completion routing, contracts and the independent hidden-alias grammar census passed. All linked tests, docs/static/type checks, package consumers and unchanged discovery/performance budgets passed. Implementation is ready for reviewed delivery; hosted review and merge remain pending."
  "2026-09-09T23:02:54.166Z","harness:codex","Reviewed closeout evidence: pm close --release-assignment closed and released both lifecycle items with resolution/expected/actual fields in the immutable close events. Live history verification passed 38 and 36 events respectively; the complete in-progress list is empty. Latest managed pm-changelog 2026.9.9 generated exactly the two new lifecycle entries under Unreleased, preserving older sections; immediate --check returned unchanged."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-09T22:43:38.132Z","harness:codex","Accepted placement: update many, close many and close delete are the canonical executable leaves; history restore and ops test-all retain the previously delivered ADR destinations. Shared alias metadata drives canonical operation identity, item addressing, bootstrap flags, completions, contracts and capabilities. Bulk aliases remain permanent and hidden; task aliases are deprecated. No gate budget or coverage threshold was relaxed."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-09T22:38:30.051Z","harness:codex","When moving executable leaves under parent verbs, normalize namespace-aware item addressing and bootstrap option ownership together with registration. Completion predicates must distinguish the parent mutation from its bulk child across every supported shell."
